<Base title="Your numbers stay with you." description="How Howloop handles calculator inputs, saved plans, email, hosting, fonts and advertising."><header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / privacy</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">HOWLOOP · THE DETAILS</span><h1 style="max-width:900px">Your numbers stay with you.</h1></header><article class="hl-wrap hl-content"><p class="hl-page-meta">Updated 4 October 2026</p><p>This policy applies to howloop.how. It describes the current calculator implementation and the advertising features that may be enabled later.</p><h2>Calculator inputs</h2><p>Calculations run in your browser. The website does not send the amounts you enter to Howloop or to a bank. We do not ask for bank logins or connect to financial accounts. The bank picker downloads public product snapshots hosted on this site.</p><h2>Saving on your device</h2><p>When you choose another language, the basic calculators temporarily carry valid inputs to that language page using this tab’s session storage. The new page reads and removes the temporary copy; copies older than 30 minutes are ignored. Amounts are not placed in the URL or sent to a translation service. Use the clear-inputs button on a language page to reset the current entries.</p><p>Choosing “Explore my savings plan” on the home page temporarily carries your inputs to the full calculator using this tab’s session storage. The calculator removes that temporary copy when it opens. Copies older than 30 minutes are ignored, and the inputs are not placed in the URL or sent to analytics.</p><p>Choosing “Save on this device” writes your calculator inputs and selected product to local storage in that browser. They remain there until you choose “Clear saved plan” or clear site data. Anyone with access to that browser profile may be able to view saved inputs. A downloaded CSV is a file on your device; manage or delete it using your device’s file controls.</p><h2>Payday Planner preview</h2><p>The 13-week cash-flow preview runs in your browser. Pay and bill labels, dates, amounts, calculated balances and shortfall indicators are not included in Howloop analytics events. Nothing saves automatically. Choosing “Save on this device” stores one plan in this browser without encryption; another person using the same browser profile may be able to restore it. “Delete saved plan” removes that saved copy, while the current working entries remain on screen. Downloads and printouts contain your entries and should be kept private.</p><p>If you allow optional analytics, Howloop measures clicks into the planner, explicit successful calculations, and optional feedback about the proposed product. These events contain only a fixed product identifier, the link placement and whether the visitor used example or edited entries. Product feedback is not an order, reservation or mailing-list signup. Events are not queued before consent. Analytics page-location values omit URL query strings and fragments, and referrer values are reduced to the referring site’s origin.</p><h2>Tax return companion</h2><p>The guided tax checklist and expense organiser runs on your device. It does not send your checklist, expense amounts or descriptions to Howloop, the ATO or an AI service. Unless you choose “Save on this device”, leaving or refreshing clears the working checklist. Saving keeps your selected answers, added expenses and unfinished expense in this browser’s local storage. It is not encrypted storage or a backup account: anyone with access to the browser profile can restore it. Use “Delete saved checklist” or clear site data to remove it. Changes are not saved automatically. Downloads are files on your device. We do not request TFNs, identity documents or myGov credentials.</p><p>If optional AI explanations are enabled, the clearly labelled panel asks for consent before sending a general question and selected topic through our hosting provider to OpenAI. Checklist selections are not sent. Enabling that panel loads Cloudflare Turnstile to protect the service, which processes technical browser and connection information. Do not include personal or financial information in a question. Howloop does not store questions in an application database and requests OpenAI responses with storage disabled; infrastructure and provider security retention may still apply. See <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data">OpenAI API data controls</a> and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>. The guided flow remains available without AI.</p><h2>Site requests and email</h2><p>The hosting provider processes ordinary connection information such as IP address, request time, browser details and the page requested to deliver and protect the site. If you email us, your email provider and ours process the message and we receive what you choose to send. Avoid sending sensitive financial or identity information. Contact us to ask about correspondence you have sent.</p><h2>Fonts and external links</h2><p>We load the DM Sans typeface from Google Fonts. The request may disclose your IP address and technical request information to Google. Links to banks, government resources and other websites take you to services with their own privacy policies.</p><h2>Site measurement</h2><p>Our hosting setup includes a Cloudflare Insights beacon for site traffic and performance measurement. It can report page visits, referral information and technical measurements such as page-loading performance. Cloudflare documents its Web Analytics service as not collecting or using visitors’ personal data. We do not attach calculator amounts, tax checklist answers or expense descriptions to analytics events. Do not put personal information in page URLs.</p><p>Google Analytics 4 is optional. Its script and analytics cookies remain off until you choose "Accept analytics" in the privacy controls at the bottom of a page. Choosing "Keep essentials", leaving the choice unanswered or disabling JavaScript keeps it off. All calculators and the tax checklist work without accepting analytics.</p><p>When allowed, Google Analytics helps us understand visitor counts, where visits come from and how pages are used. Google may receive page addresses, referral information, device details and approximate location, and use cookies to distinguish visits. Google signals and advertising personalisation signals are disabled. We do not send calculator amounts, tax checklist answers or expense descriptions, and do not use this measurement to identify visitors by name.</p><p>Your choice and the time you made it are stored in this browser under "howloop-analytics-choice-v1". If browser storage is unavailable, the choice applies only to the current page visit. Use "Privacy choices" at the bottom of any page to change your selection. Withdrawing permission disables further measurement and clears accessible Google Analytics cookies for this site; use the offered reload button to unload the script. Withdrawing does not remove information already sent to Google. Clearing site data removes the stored choice and resets analytics to off.</p><p>Read <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/about/">Cloudflare’s analytics explanation</a>, <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>. Page measurement is separate from saving a calculator or checklist on your device.</p><h2>Cookies and advertising</h2><p>The current release does not load advertising scripts. Cloudflare Insights measures site use as described above. Google Analytics 4 runs only after your analytics opt-in. The privacy choice uses local storage to remember your selection; saved plans use it only when you choose to save. We may introduce Google AdSense after completing account and site setup.</p><p>If Google ads are enabled, Google and other advertising vendors may use cookies to serve ads based on visits to this and other websites. Google’s advertising cookies can support personalised ads. You can manage personalisation at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads">Google Ads Settings</a> and find third-party choices at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">YourAdChoices</a>. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from partner sites</a>.</p><p>Before advertising is enabled, this policy and consent controls must reflect the actual setup. The analytics controls described here are not an advertising consent platform. Applicable regional advertising consent requirements, including Google's certified consent-platform requirements for relevant European traffic, must be configured before those ads are enabled.</p><h2>Contact and changes</h2><p>For privacy questions or requests about correspondence, email <a href="mailto:hello@howloop.how">hello@howloop.how</a>. Browser-stored calculator inputs can be removed directly on your device. This policy will be updated when the site’s data practices change.</p></article></Base>
